<resources>
    <!--
      The Spanish interface (REQ-206, D5, AD-15).

      Register and conventions, so a later string is written the same way:

      * Second person informal ("tú"), like the English original's direct
        address and like Android's own Spanish. Never "usted".
      * Neutral Spanish: no regionalism that would read as foreign anywhere
        the owner's library is read. "Añadir", not "agregar"; "ordenador"
        never appears because the app says "dispositivo".
      * Plain and honest, the same rule the English copy follows: no word
        promises more than the build does. In particular the app says
        "quitar" (take out of the library) and never "eliminar" or "borrar"
        for a book, because it never deletes a reader's file.
      * "ppm" — palabras por minuto — is the Spanish reading-speed unit and
        replaces "WPM" everywhere it appears, including inside sentences.
      * FastReader, EPUB, TalkBack, Android, DRM and CC0 are product names
        or standards and stay as they are.

      The crash report itself is deliberately NOT translated: see the
      comment on `crash_offer_title` below and `CrashReport.kt`.

      Completeness is a build gate, not a convention: `MissingTranslation`,
      `ExtraTranslation` and `MissingQuantity` are lint errors (see the
      `lint` block in app/build.gradle.kts), so a string added to
      `values/strings.xml` without a line here fails CI rather than falling
      back to English on a Spanish device.
    -->
