    <!-- Added folders (REQ-104).

         Spanish has a CLDR "many" plural category that English does not: a
         count that is a whole number of millions takes "de" before the noun
         ("2.000.000 de libros", but "5 libros"). Nobody will own a million
         books, yet the category is part of a complete Spanish resource and
         `MissingQuantity` is a gate here, so it is written rather than left
         to fall back. Where the number sits inside parentheses no "de" is
         possible, so those two items are identical on purpose. -->
